      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a comprehensive list of test cases designed to maximize coverage depth for your \"CyberShield NextGen\" module. These cover functionality, state, filtering, and logging thoroughly.\n\n*   Verify inbound TCP traffic is allowed when explicitly permitted by a rule.\n*   Verify outbound TCP traffic is permitted when explicitly allowed by a rule.\n*   Test stateful inspection by allowing an initial connection and confirming subsequent return traffic is permitted automatically.\n*   Test SPI failure by attempting to inject unsolicited inbound packets to an established outbound session.\n*   Validate the rule-based engine by allowing traffic based on specific source IP addresses.\n*   Validate the rule-based engine by allowing traffic based on specific destination ports.\n*   Validate protocol filtering by explicitly allowing UDP traffic while denying TCP on the same port.\n*   Test maximum rule load: apply 256 rules and ensure performance remains stable.\n*   Test rule precedence: verify the first matching rule is applied correctly, even if later rules conflict.\n*   Trigger a denial event and verify that an entry is precisely logged to the local syslog.\n*   Test logging robustness by rapidly sending many denied packets to ensure the syslog buffer handles the load.\n*   Verify",
      "source": "target",
